  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Sudan Community Schools Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Children in South Sudan have missed out on years of schooling because of the war. The government doesn&apos;t have the money to provide school places for all the children who need them. In addition, even where schools exist, children can be put off going to them by threats of violence from other children, corporal punishment from teachers, or the lack of basic facilities such as toilets. Girls and vulnerable groups, like orphans and disabled children, particularly suffer a loss in education. The project will set up  &#x2018;one room schools&apos; in a number of remote areas; children will be taught in a special room set aside in their communities by women who come from their area and who have been trained by the project on how to teach. Because of this project, many children and young people will be given a chance to have an education which they could never otherwise have enjoyed. Afterwards, they can then carry on with their education by joining government schools; or take up vocational training or start small businesses. The project can lead to life-changing opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
